        "comments": "The assembly bFalTin1.hap2.1 is based on 66x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. This genome has been assembled using PacBio and HiC data and phased. The result is two curated haplotypes. The microchromosomes were identified through two stage curation of scaffolds smaller than 20 Mbp, combined with homology-based identification using known microchromosome genes via Microfinder. The Z and W chromosomes were identified based on its single-copy status within a diploid assembly. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 1 (119,327 - 120,906 Kbp) are unknown. A haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 4 (98,667 -113,013 bp).Chromosome 6 shows heterozygous rearrangements. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 3 (121,554 - 122,506 Kbp) are unknown. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome W (7,828 - 13,104 & 31,399 - 47,207 Kbp) are unknown. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome Z (75,039 - 76,834 & 78,456 - 80,121 Kbp) are unknown.",
